From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenROAD <openroad@openroad.tools>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tomlplusplus: pin the archive's checksum

tomlplusplus_ext declares the tomlplusplus http_archive without a
checksum, so nothing verifies the download, and neither Bazel's
repository cache nor a remote downloader can serve it by hash. A build
that routes downloads through a remote cache's Remote Asset API
(--experimental_remote_downloader) then makes the cache download the
archive again on every fetch.

Pin the integrity of the v3.4.0 tag archive. It is the value Bazel
reports for the unpinned download ("indicated that a canonical
reproducible form can be obtained by modifying arguments integrity =
..."), and the archive from GitHub and from the BCR's Cloudflare mirror
both hash to it.
---
diff --git a/dependency_support/tomlplusplus_ext.bzl b/dependency_support/tomlplusplus_ext.bzl
--- a/dependency_support/tomlplusplus_ext.bzl
+++ b/dependency_support/tomlplusplus_ext.bzl
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
     http_archive(
         name = "tomlplusplus",
         urls = ["https://github.com/marzer/tomlplusplus/archive/refs/tags/v3.4.0.tar.gz"],
+        integrity = "sha256-hRf2WTik+q6cz467NmMaOMHK37XvqF2acuFbnpfSUVU=",
         strip_prefix = "tomlplusplus-3.4.0",
         build_file = "//:dependency_support/tomlplusplus.BUILD.bazel",
     )
